  /*
  The key values here use the enums integral type so we use integers for keys.
  Also the ordering is important here, it is based on the enum's ordering in the source code.
  So additions have to be made to the end and a reorder will result in completely different values.
  Hence we have to be very careful while making additions/changes here. 
  On the other hand, these tradeoffs allows us to have no middle-mapping layer and a couple of other upsides:
  Constant time element access using enumerators as indices and labels being actually "ordered" (duh).
  We can go straight from enums to translation values in each file, using no middle key values.
  So no C++ container for mapping enums to json key values which is super nice.
  */
